# 🔹 Mode A — Deterministic Projection (Live in SEU V10)

This mode is already implemented.

It derives forward advisory directly from:
* ERI_Flow (start, end, delta, % movement)
* EVI_Flow (volatility shift)
* ES_Flow (band migration)
* Emotion_Flow (dominant shifts + polarity shifts)
* Pattern_Flow (macro classification)
* RF tier pressure dynamics
* PEM_Guidance

This layer produces:
* Trajectory classification (CRISIS / RECOVERY / STABLE / VOLATILE)
* Structural instability signals
* Escalation likelihood classification
* Intervention window sensitivity
* Stream bias recommendation (Fix / Stabilize / Amplify orientation)
* Risk band advisory

Characteristics:
* Fully explainable
* Deterministic
* Governance-safe
* No probabilistic calibration
* No statistical inference
* No state mutation

This mode extends the SEU forward without altering it.

It is structural extrapolation, not ML prediction.

---

# 🔹 Mode B — Statistical Calibration (Optional Extension)
This mode overlays probabilistic modeling on canonical SEU snapshots. It operates strictly on versioned, 
append-only SEU history.

### Possible Targets

#### Binary
* ES downgrade within X days
* ES upgrade within X days
* Crisis trigger within X days
* Urgency escalation within X days
* EVI high-tier entry within X days

#### Multiclass
* Next ES Band (ES1–ES5)
* Next Pattern classification
* Next RF urgency tier

#### Regression
* ERI delta next window
* EVI delta next window

#### Time-to-Event
* Days until ES4
* Days until ES5
* Days until P0

### Mandatory Methodological Discipline

Statistical Surface 1 must:
* Use time-ordered splits (no random leakage)
* Align horizon labels consistently
* Separate competing crisis risks (ES4 vs ES5)
* Enforce minimum positive event thresholds
* Respect snapshot cadence variability
* Fail loudly if duration fields are missing
* Never mutate SEU state

Statistical calibration enhances precision.
It does not redefine ontology.

